data.solution:
(i) The integers greater than 1 and less than or equal to 4 are 2, 3, 4. So, A = {2, 3, 4}.
(ii) The number of elements in A is 3. So, n(A) = 3.
(iii) The number of all subsets of A is 2^(n(A)) = 2^3 = 8.
The subsets are:
Ø
{2}, {3}, {4}
{2, 3}, {2, 4}, {3, 4}
{2, 3, 4}
Proper subsets are all subsets except the set A itself.
So, proper subsets are: Ø, {2}, {3}, {4}, {2, 3}, {2, 4}, {3, 4}.

